<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Upper March</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Upper March of al-Andalus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Upper March was the north-eastern frontier province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, facing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> and the Christian kingdoms of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>. Local dynasties such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-qasi">Banu Qasi</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tudela">Tudela</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tujibids">Tujibids</a> dominated it. After the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> it became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of Zaragoza, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Lleida</a> as a major town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/upper-march.jpg" alt="Upper March" width="320" height="277" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: File:Califato de Córdoba - 1000.svg: Tyk (talk · contribs) derivative work: Morningstar1814 (talk · contribs) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Califato_de_C%C3%B3rdoba_-_1000-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
